  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuberculosis - Togo (01-Jan-2008-31-Dec-2012)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB is a significant public health problem in Togo.  The overall goal of the program supported by this grant is to reduce TB-related illness and death by improving the quality of DOTS services throughout the service delivery chain. The program targets TB patients and their families, prisoners and the wider community. Grant funds are being used to strengthen the community-based DOTS approach through training community health workers; provide TB treatment to patients in prisons, in the armed forces, clinics and enterprises; develop information and campaign material to sensitize the public, family member, civil society, private clinics and enterprises as well as key opinion leaders and the media; and increase prevention activities among vulnerable populations.</narrative>
  </description>
